  "result": "**Final verdict: `OK`** (gate run 2 of 6).\n\n**The body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/left_turn.lean`):\n\n```lean\ndef onset : Formula := .cmp (.measure \"kin_yaw_rate\" [aU]) .gt pOnsetYawRate\ndef headingChange : Term := .headingSince \"u\" pHeadingStep onset\ndef body : Formula := .cmp headingChange .ge pTurnAngle\n```\n\nThe contract's sentences on the extent and the history are `headingSince`'s own semantics — true when the accumulated change first reaches the angle, still true while it holds it, restarted at a later onset, and unknown (never false) where no onset is observed with the rate known since, where an interval exceeds the heading step, or where a rate since the onset is missing — so the whole contract is written with the one claimed atom and the three formal parameters, no literal of its own.\n\n**One narrowing declared**: \"first rose above the onset yaw rate\" is read as the *latest* definite rise before the judged observation, which the contract's own \"until a later onset starts the count again\" directs.\n\n**Witnesses**: one car, ten observations 500 ms apart; heading step 500 ms, onset rate 5 deg/s, turn angle 45 deg. `holds` reaches 45 deg at t = 2500, a second and a half after the onset at t = 1000, and holds it to the end (window 2500–4500, since the trace's first observation can never be an onset and the observations before the angle are false by the contract); `fails` is a lane change peaking at 12 deg; `blind` is a car already turning at the first observation with `kin.yaw_rate` masked.\n\n**Gate run 1 was `WITNESS_FAIL`** — not the body, but the trace lint: my scenes held a heading constant across an interval whose yaw rate would have turned it. I rebuilt all three traces so each heading is the previous one turned by that observation's rate, with positions following at 5 m an observation. Run 2 returned `OK`.\n\nReport written to `/local-scratch2/sma407/scratch_core/launch/remote/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/demo22-1109-0108/iter-001/code/concept__drv_motion_left_turn/task_result.md`.",
